{% set local_problem %}
<p>Scottsboro area homes face a debris onslaught from multiple directions. Pine trees drop needles year-round. Hardwoods shed leaves every fall. And the lakeside location means additional organic debris blowing in from the water.</p>

<p>For full-time residents, this means climbing ladders 3-4 times a year or paying $150-200+ per cleaning. Annoying, but manageable.</p>

<p>For vacation homeowners, it's worse. Gutters can clog, overflow, and cause damage while you're away — and you won't know until your next visit. By then, what started as a minor clog may have become foundation damage, fascia rot, or landscape erosion.</p>

<p>Gutter guards solve this problem permanently. Debris stays out, water flows through, and your gutters work properly whether you're there to check on them or not.</p>
{% endset %}

{% set service_explanation %}
<p>Gutter guards are protective covers or screens that fit over or inside your gutters. They allow water to enter while blocking leaves, pine needles, and other debris.</p>

<p>Different types work better for different situations. Micro-mesh guards excel at blocking fine debris like pine needles. Screen guards handle larger leaves effectively. Solid covers use surface tension to pull water in while debris slides off.</p>

<p>For Scottsboro's mix of pine and hardwood debris, we typically recommend micro-mesh guards — they handle both fine needles and larger leaves while maintaining good water flow during heavy rains.</p>
{% endset %}

{% set why_us %}
